{"id": "sllama0002", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A deer uses its speed and agility to escape from predator s, running quickly through the forest or over open ground. Some species also have sharp hooves that can be used for defense if they feel threatened.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0010", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for uranium is U. It' s derived from the Latin word uran us, which was named after the planet Uran us.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 7, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0018", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The Olympic sport that requires athletes to hit a target with a bow and arrow is called archery.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0026", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for lithium is Li.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0034", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The currency used in Canada is the Canadian dollar. It' s often abbreviated as CA D or referred to simply as the loon ie because of the loonie coin, which features a loon on one side.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 12, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0042", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The smallest country in the world is Vat ica City. It is located within Rome, Italy, and has an area of just about 0. 49 square kilometers, or roughly 1/7 th of a square mile. Despite its tiny size, it is home to around 8 00 people and serves as the center for the Catholic Church with St. Peter ’s Basilica being one of its most famous sites.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 24, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0050", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There are 33 bones in the human spine.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0058", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The highest mountain peak in North America is Den al, which is part of the Alaska Range in Alaska. It reaches an elevation of about 20,3 17 feet, or approximately 6,1 90 meters above sea level.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0066", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The Golden Gate Bridge is located in San Francisco, California. It' s one of the most iconic landmarks in the United States and a symbol of the city itself.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0074", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Mark Zuckerberg is the founder of Facebook.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0082", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The lead singer of Queen is F reddie Mercury. He was the band' s frontman and known for his powerful, dramatic vocals and flamboyant stage presence.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0090", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The main character in the movie The Ma trix is named T homas And erson, but he later becomes known as Neo.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0098", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The average human has three layers of skin. These are the epidermis, the dermis, and the hypo dermis. Each layer plays a unique role in protecting our bodies from harm, regulating temperature, and maintaining overall health.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0106", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The oldest Olympic champion in any sport is swimmer Mis ha Alo kov, who won a gold medal at the age of 41 years and 28 days during the 195 6 Melbourne Summer Olympics.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0114", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A hexagon has six sides.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0122", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The bone that can't be moved is the skull bone. It's fixed in place to protect your brain, so you can't move it like other bones in your body.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0130", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The capital of Israel is Jerusalem.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0138", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The body's natural defense against infection and disease is the immune system. It' s made up of white blood cells, antibodies, and other components that work together to protect us from harmful microorganism s like bacteria and virus es.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0146", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Hanukkah lasts eight days.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 2, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0154", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The only tennis player to hold all four Grand Slam titles simultaneously is Ste fan Edberg. He achieved this rare feat in 1 9 88, winning the Australian Open, French Open, Wimbled on, and US Open in the same year.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0162", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for oxygen is O.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0170", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Neil Armstrong was the first person to walk on the moon.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0178", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The smallest bone in the human body is the stapes. It's found in the middle ear and plays a crucial role in hearing by helping to transmit sound waves from the eardrum to the inner ear. It' s incredibly tiny, about the size of a grain of rice, but it' s essential for our ability to hear.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0186", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Tea is made from the leaves of the tea plant.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0194", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The lightest element in the periodic table is hydrogen. It has only one proton and one electron, making it the simplest atom.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0202", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Nine minus five is four.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 2, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0210", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The historical found er of Buddhism is Siddhartha Gu atama, who lived in ancient India around the 5th or 6th century BCE. He is also known as the Buddha, which means the Enlightened One. After experiencing suffering and seeking enlightenment, he developed a path to end suffering called the Four Noble Truth s and the Eightfold Path. His teachings formed the foundation of Buddhist philosophy and practice.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 23, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0218", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Hydrogen is represented by the symbol H. It is the lightest and most abundant element in the universe, found in water and many organic compound s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0226", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A human has two eyes. One on each side of the face, allowing us to see in both directions at once and providing depth perception.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0234", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A bat uses echolocation to find food. It sends out high-pitched sound waves that bounce off objects and return as echo es. By listening to these echoes, the bat can figure out where things are, how far away they are, and even what they look like in the dark. This helps it catch insects or other prey at night when it's hard to see.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 23, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0242", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Tobey Maguire played Sp ider-Man in the first three films. Then Andrew Gar field took over for a few more movies, and now Tom Hol land is playing Spider-M an in the Marvel Cin ema Universe.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
